WEBVTT

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.120
A road like this should be used
for everyone to evacuate!

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.880
So, the government foresaw
things would come to this?

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.030
If so, why did turn its
back on its own people?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.350
Yo, Hibiki.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.540
This is under the Diet Building?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.160
Impossible!

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.510
This is the Byakko's summoner?

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.360
Sir!

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.250
Hey! Please open up.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.620
You're okay doing this to minors?! Hey!

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.330
Why did they have to capture us?

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:54.250
Because we called forth that demon.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.340
Nitta...

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.590
I'm sure our mothers are worried.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.550
I bet this is some kind of mistake.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.910
They'll clear things up soon.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:11.520
Hibiki...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.530
What's happened to us?

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.030
Why was only I brought here?

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.240
Because I want you alone
to know the truth.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:46.230
What is this? What are they doing?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:50.640
We are a secret organization attached
to the Japanese government,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.520
the Japan Meteorological Agency: JP's.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:56.600
I am Commander Makoto Sako.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.520
JP's?

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.290
JP's has long overseen Japan's barriers,
protected its distinguished citizens.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:05.340
Barriers?

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.660
Defense systems composed
of spiritual energy.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:12.080
If they ceased to be maintained,
it would allow various enemies to invade.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.900
Enemies? From foreign countries?

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:15.700
No.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.540
They're difficult for the layperson to perceive,
but they definitely exist...

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.630
The anomalous races.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.590
Like, ghosts and demons?

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:30.250
They're called different names, but for now,
you may regard them as such.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:37.350
Up till now, there's no way I could
have believed this. But...

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.410
I summoned a demon and fought.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.070
Yes.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.090
You summoned Byakko,
an Avatar and one of

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.820
the Four Symbols of the Chinese constellations.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.890
It's no small fry a
commoner can call forth.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.290
This is JP's bureau chief.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.690
Yamato Hotsuin.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.380
I'm the one who called you here.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.430
Hibiki Kuze: No summoner at the

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:12.030
Tokyo bureau can call forth
anything to match it.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.100
It's not like that power...

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.270
Is something you wanted, eh?

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.030
The power to call forth demons...

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.480
It exists.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.490
There have been various methods to
summon demons since antiquity.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.730
We've broken down "sorcery"
into mathematical formulae

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:30.820
and successfully made use of the demons.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.330
The Demon Summoning app!

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.290
Naturally, it's not something the
general public should possess.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.070
Why was something that dangerous
put on our cell phones?

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:42.990
We don't know the source.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.600
We're still looking into it.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:50.000
We've been preparing for
the calamity of today.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:55.310
So, you knew that something
like that would happen?

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:59.890
Then you could have warned people,
had them evacuate, right?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.650
That would have caused undue panic
and interfered with our operations.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.530
That's selfish, isn't it?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.360
It's our only choice right now.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.490
To think, you all have this facility
but aren't helping anyone...

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.830
Just what are you up to?

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.920
The one you defeated today was
nothing more than a small fry.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.980
Six enemies remain.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.240
We have six days.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.500
Unless we defeat all
enemies that manifest,

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.680
our world will be eaten away...

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.030
and disappear.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.220
Disappear?

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.300
Just as he said. The
world will be no more.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.980
And who are these enemies?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:50.610
The aggressors...

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.610
Septentrion.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.870
The Septentrion are
of a different world.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.170
They can only be defeated
through demonic power.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.750
You have that power.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.220
Won't you help us?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.110
Obey me, Hibiki Kuze.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.430
As the report said,

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.820
this is completely different from our
Demon Summoning program.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.410
What is this doing in the hands
of the general public?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.520
Beats me. I can't get hold
of Prof. Kanno either,

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.950
so right now we're at a standstill.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:39.330
It assesses the user's ability and
converts that to a figure.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.300
That's then used to bid
at a "Demon Auction."

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:44.670
What a ghastly interface.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.960
Don't use it carelessly!

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.950
That's much more intense than ours.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.750
Unless you're a powerful summoner,
any demon that appears will kill you!

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.550
Just who made this thing?

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.030
Dubhe has been defeated.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.730
What do you think?

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:08.560
Was it luck?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:13.080
Or was that also human potential?

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.630
An organization that
has prepared for war...

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.280
The power to summon demons
and use them as weapons...

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:24.660
Kuze?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.510
Did I wake you? Sorry.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:28.540
No.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.180
Did you sleep a little?

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.020
Yes.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.020
What...

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.460
will to happen to us?

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.570
Nothing will happen.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.360
If we do nothing, that is.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.810
What do you mean?

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:47.610
It means this is over with.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:51.360
They just wanted to
inspect our cell phones.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.760
Oh, really? Thank goodness.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.500
We will be released.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:09:59.870
But...

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.340
This world will be eaten away...

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:06.380
and disappear.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.870
If that's true...

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.060
There's nowhere to run, is there?

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:30.290
Hibiki, they're really gonna
let us go home, right?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.280
Yeah.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.730
Thank goodness.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:35.610
I'll take you two to Ariake.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.900
That's the deal.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.660
Huh? "Deal"?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.660
Kuze, what's going on?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.300
It's not like I made a deal.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.050
I just said that unless they
release you two unharmed,

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:49.620
I couldn't possibly imagine
cooperating with them.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.640
Wait a minute! "Cooperate"?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.840
You plan to stay with them?

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.640
Hey, Hibiki!

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.890
I have the power to fight.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.540
Hibiki...

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.370
You can study, but that doesn't mean you

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.100
have to be good at fighting, right?

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.410
Mother!

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.430
The heck is this?

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.800
It seems our road info is mixed up.

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:52.280
Let's look for another route.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.990
I'll go on my own.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.860
Nitta! What are you saying?

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.660
You can't walk there.
We'll give you a ride.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:04.990
It's fine.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:05.880
Let's...

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.240
Let's at least go to the
emergency shelter together.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:13.540
If it's close to Ariake,
we could get some information.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:15.710
Kuze...

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.560
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.470
We should stay together.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.510
Miss Sako, will the car be all right?

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.390
Yes, it's fine.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.950
The trains aren't running and
we're not getting any news.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.820
I wonder how the other areas are.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.200
If only we could use the Net...

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:45.790
This way, Mr. Devil!

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.840
Hey, quiet down!
This way, Mr. Devil!

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:51.870
I'm gonna go walk and take a look.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.640
I see. Take care.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:55.250
Yeah.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.210
I'll go check upstairs.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:05.140
Understood.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.140
We'll be there soon.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:13.590
Um, you can help these
people evacuate, right?

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.150
JP's is neither police nor firefighters.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.530
We have a mission of our own.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.740
Don't you think you're
only helping yourselves?

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:25.320
Uh, never mind.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.940
This is as far as I can take you.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:35.120
I'm sorry you got dragged into this.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.500
I'll give these back.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.550
We've rigged them to connect
to a special JP's line.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.300
If something happens, contact us.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.380
All right then. Be careful.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:54.880
I'm telling you, demons did this!

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:55.900
What are you talking about?

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:59.170
I saw them. Demons eating humans!

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.030
The demons caused this whole disaster!

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:03.500
Actually, I also--

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.030
Stop it already!

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:07.110
You learn anything?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.100
No.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.630
This is going nowhere.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.940
Um, do you know what's
happened in Ariake?

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.680
No, I don't.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.830
Right now, all you can
see there is dirt clouds.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.800
I'll get something to drink.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.690
Okay.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:54.990
I'm doing it, if it will help us.

00:15:20.590 --> 00:15:21.620
Please.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:23.420
Please!

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.620
Thank you!

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.170
I got some.

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:38.080
Good job. If you hang in
there, God will provide.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.060
Yeah!

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:41.380
God, huh?

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.990
Mom, I wanna go home!

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.220
Mother!

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.420
A demon!

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:25.330
No!

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.470
Brother!

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.490
I can't count on anyone else. Think.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.940
What's the best thing I can do?

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.950
Byakko! Take that thing outside!

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.790
What's that?

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.560
Byakko!

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:33.650
Hibiki!

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:36.450
Byakko!

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.470
Dammit. Hibiki! I'll help you!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.000
Huh?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.840
What's this? "Under repair"?

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.320
Hibiki!

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:51.040
Daichi, get out of here with the others.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.420
Idiot! How could I leave you here?!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.220
I'll be fine. I have Byakko.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:18:00.260
No matter how strong that thing is,
why do you have to fight?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.640
Everything was normal up till yesterday.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:09.270
We're just high-school students, right?

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:12.190
Why did all this happen?!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.280
Looking away now...

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.280
will lead to regret!

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.240
Hibiki!

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.660
There's more? There's no end to them!

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:31.290
You okay?

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.670
Miss Sako! What's that?

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.650
It's a Divine, a Power in my employ.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:42.880
More importantly, I
don't see any summoners.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.300
A cell phone must be running
amuck somewhere.

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.420
Then I'll handle things here.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:47.980
Please do.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:56.360
True enough, I didn't want this power.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:08.080
But if I can help save
others, then running away...

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.750
is something I can't do!

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.230
Situation contained.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:44.840
Nitta!

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:46.130
Where's Kuze?

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.430
He stood up?!

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:54.790
Now he'll attack US, too?

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.800
"Big brother"!

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:01.970
Thank you!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.310
Hibiki Kuze.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:13.150
You are wise indeed.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:15.700
The world could disappear?

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.310
I still don't really understand.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:25.160
But if my power can be of use,
if I can fight in to help others...

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:28.450
I'll do everything I can.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:33.280
We're grateful for your help, too.

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:35.760
W-We heard the details.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.840
The world's in trouble, huh?

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.840
So you finally understand?

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:43.270
I can't leave Hibiki on his own!

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:44.430
I...

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:48.460
When Kuze was fighting,
there was nothing I could do.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:51.240
I just cried.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.690
There's no way that's right!

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:57.010
It's fine. Thank you, Nitta.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.900
So, what do we all do now?

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.070
Makoto.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:02.870
Sir.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.580
Put it on the main monitor!

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:08.450
Prof. Fumi Kanno.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:12.330
She's the scientist in charge of JP's
security and summoning systems.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:15.270
Huh? That girl is?

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:18.170
She was on standby at
the Osaka main office,

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:21.770
but she disappeared at the same
time the Septentrion showed up.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.340
She had an accident?

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.300
That's not possible.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:29.880
Losing Prof. Kanno hinders
our upcoming plans.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:33.930
You all will join our
search party and find her.

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:36.780
Those are your first orders.

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:06.980
I have not thought about living until yesterday

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:15.460
It just seems like one scene of a film

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.620
I need lore!

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:23.800
Oh, everything has utterly changed now

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:26.610
Nakisou ni naru kurai

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:29.110
Me o fusaidemo kawaranai

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.350
Omoide ga hanpirei

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:32.900
I take it!

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:34.850
Close your eyes

00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:36.950
Imagine how to live

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:38.620
You must do it

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:40.320
I close my eyes

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:43.810
And determined, I'm pressed for choice

00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:46.660
Just about to leave, far away

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:49.500
Ikiru tame, it's only one

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:52.870
We gotta choose it, so do we?

00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:54.970
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:57.540
Just about to leave, far away

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:00.410
Ikiru tame, it's only one

00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:04.310
Can you drive your destiny?

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:05.840
Now

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:15.550
Hey.

00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:17.530
What do you want now?

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.870
We have no more use for you.

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:21.140
That's true, isn't it?

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:25.300
Incidentally, are you all right not
keeping him by your side?

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:28.300
There's no need,
if they seem the type to not die easily.

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:30.980
Oh, really? So you have high hopes.

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:33.650
Then maybe I'll be hopeful as well...

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:36.800
For something new that sparkles.

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.360
Per the covenant of antiquity...

00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:51.030
JP's has finally moved to action, eh?

00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:53.040
